# tools/co/color_ramp_witness.rish -- a piecewise-linear ramp across many control colors proves itself on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- the multi-stop gradient beside the two-endpoint ramp (image/color_gradient.rye) and
# the open color algebra (image/color.rye).
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260816/20260816-210735_season-g-color-algebra-crux.md (the color floor this stands on).
# Teacher, thanked clean-room: gratitude/w3c-css-color.md (the W3C CSS Color spec + sRGB -- public standards only).
#
# The crux this witness proves is the general form of the two-color gradient: grow a piecewise-linear ramp across K
# evenly-spaced control colors, written as a single-stranded consumer of color's own blend. dst[0] is the first control
# exactly, dst[len-1] the last, and a stop that lands on a control reads it byte-for-byte. The general contains the
# special -- a two-control ramp equals color_gradient.gradient byte-for-byte. A black-grey-white ramp ascends
# non-decreasing in luminance across both segments; a color-to-itself ramp stays flat; too few controls or an
# out-of-band length refuse by name. No new color maths -- a mix routed to its segment, so color's own proofs carry
# through. No network, no key, no funds -- the multi-stop gradient Brushstroke and Skate paint the day the design system
# lands.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/co/color_ramp_witness.rish

say "color-ramp: Language EN -- Season G's multi-stop gradient; a keeper names a list of control colors and reads back an evenly-spaced ramp that passes through each one, the CSS multi-stop linear-gradient on our own color model."
say "color-ramp: Style Radiant -- compose not braid; color DECIDES the blend and this module only routes each stop to its segment, so a ramp is a color.mix within a segment and the two-control ramp is exactly the two-endpoint gradient."
say "color-ramp: Lens TAME -- u32 control and stop counts bounded by ramp_max_control and the shared gradient ceiling; the segment routing in u32 so it never wraps; endpoints and byte range asserted; integer fixed-point so a ramp is deterministic; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/color_ramp"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/color_ramp.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "color-ramp: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "color-ramp: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "color-ramp: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-color-ramp" else "color-ramp: selftest did not print the GREEN color-ramp line"

assert selftest.out contains "the general contains the special" else "color-ramp: the two-control ramp did not prove equal to the gradient"

say "color-ramp: GREEN -- a multi-stop ramp passes through its controls and contains the two-color gradient, proven on metal."
